Package: coursepack
Title: Build Canvas Course Packages from Plain-Text Course Sources
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Logan", "Kelly", email = "logan.kelly@uwrf.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build tools for plain-text course authoring. Turns a course's
    declarative manifests into a Canvas-importable Common Cartridge, a QTI 1.2
    quiz package, and a local browsable preview, and audits the rendered course
    against WCAG 2.1 AA. Course content never enters the package. Every entry
    point takes the course project root as its first argument, so one installed
    copy serves any number of courses without any of them being able to see
    another.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    digest,
    grDevices,
    grid,
    jsonlite,
    magick,
    stats,
    stringr,
    tools,
    utils,
    xml2,
    yaml
Suggests:
    exams,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Node.js with npx, for the accessibility audit only. pa11y
    9.1.1 is fetched at run time by npx and is not vendored. pa11y needs a
    Chrome or Chromium binary for its headless browser. None of this is needed
    to build a cartridge, a QTI package, or a preview.
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
